WEBVTT

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:03.350
KISS! KISS! I’m in love.

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:10.620
This never-ending LOOP,

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:13.840
a cycle that goes out of spin,

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:17.270
and runs towards you.

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:23.740
Under this bright sunlight,

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:27.040
and blue sky,

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:30.540
I’m accelerating so fast that I can’t stop moving.

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:35.690
It’s my first time having these feelings.

00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:40.450
What should I do? My throbbing heart doesn’t know,

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:46.590
and keeps searching for the solution, even now.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:49.720
KISS! KISS! I’m in love.

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:53.400
I am here because of your kiss,

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:56.350
which has stopped the flow of time.

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:59.870
I knock on the door to your heart,

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:02.870
and watch your wavering dreams.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:06.640
Your RUBY eyes are what absorb me in.

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:09.550
Barely in sight,

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:15.880
the translucent door to your heart looks like it is opening now.

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:20.400
Only you...

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:23.830
my kiss will reach...

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:42.330
Wake up, Nana!

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:44.330
Nana!

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:45.290
Okay.

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:56.470
Oh, you're early.

00:01:56.470 --> 00:01:57.510
Leaving already?

00:01:57.510 --> 00:01:59.010
Yeah, I have something to do.

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:03.140
I'm leaving now.

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:36.300
Hey...

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:41.340
I'm sorry about the other day.

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:45.770
You just came to apologize because it made you uneasy, right?

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:47.220
That's not it!

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:50.810
It's just as you said, Sakino.

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:53.610
I was halfhearted with everything.

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:57.030
So, I thought I'd try to change a little.

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:02.530
I won't forgive you if you become halfhearted again, okay?

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:03.910
Y-Yeah!

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:13.710
Is everyone prepared?

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:19.300
Your first midterm as third years is coming up, so keep that in mind.

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:23.090
If you don't do well, it'll hurt you later on.

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:24.760
The time...

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:26.310
Mizusawa.

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:28.060
Has finally come.

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:29.810
Mizusawa.

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:33.650
What's wrong, you look pale?

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:36.610
Ah, really, you think so?

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:41.820
Anyway, can I come to your store again?

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:43.740
The other time was really fun.

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:46.830
Yeah, Master was really happy.

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:47.870
He said to bring you again.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:51.660
Really, then maybe I'll go there today!

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:55.460
Ah, no.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:57.460
What about studying for the test, though?

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:00.800
I think it'll be okay.

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:03.630
The test is next week anyway.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:06.260
Then let's meet after school, at the gates.

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:07.510
Okay.

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:22.490
Do you know where Kazuki is, Sakino-san?

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:25.280
It looked like he left in a hurry.

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:28.160
Geez, I thought he was going to practice with me during lunch.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:29.540
Sakino, come here!

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:31.040
Yes!

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:41.800
I guess I'll eat first then.

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:51.350
I guess I can't invite her yet.

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:04.820
Um, how long are we-

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:05.570
Be quiet.

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:09.370
That's enough.

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:13.000
No good, this is a failure.

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:16.500
My heart rate isn't rising at all.

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:17.750
Really?

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:22.420
I thought I'd sterilize the situation before the kissing stage by staring at you.

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:24.340
I wonder what went wrong?

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:28.430
Perhaps we should try kissing again.

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:29.390
Eh?!

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:30.850
No, that's not it.

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:36.270
For now, I'll think on the matter again.

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:38.060
We'll take a break from the experiment.

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:42.940
Students are prohibited from being here while tests are being conducted.

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:43.860
Didn't you know?

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:45.280
Oh, I see.

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:50.030
What are you going to do about the test, Futami-san?

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:51.450
What do you mean?

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:53.660
Are you going to hand in a blank sheet again?

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:57.210
Who knows?

00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:00.000
I'll decide depending on how I feel.

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:13.100
F-Futami-san, what's this drink that tingles my tongue?!

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:14.560
It's coffee.

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:37.080
It's just not coming together.

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:41.080
Maybe, you're too concerned about the setting?

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:45.340
I'm sorry, that was unnecessary.

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:47.090
No, please let me hear it.

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:51.800
Um, you've been using a lot of stories as reference,

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:54.810
so you might have been thinking that it has to be elaborate.

00:06:55.810 --> 00:06:58.890
It might be better to make it life-sized.

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:02.060
Life-sized, huh?

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:04.940
I guess you would call it a short story?

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:07.150
I can't explain it well.

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:08.860
I see.

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:11.910
I got it, that might be more realistic.

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:13.950
Thank you, Hoshino-san.

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:16.200
It's nothing.

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:24.710
Sakino!

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:28.300
Hey, you're going to your club, right?

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:30.880
I'll help you with your private training afterwards.

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:33.970
Sorry, I can't today.

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:39.810
Later.

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:42.810
What's up with her?

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:46.020
I'm home.

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:56.160
Huh, Mao-neechan hasn't come back yet.

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:02.080
Did you listen to that CD I lent you the other day?

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:04.380
Yeah, it was really good!

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:07.540
I have another version of it, so I'll lend it to you.

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:09.000
Okay, thanks!

00:08:14.930 --> 00:08:16.760
I asked you this before,

00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:20.390
but you're not going to a university, right?

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:22.690
Yeah, that's my plan.

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:24.060
What about you?

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:27.060
What should I do?

00:08:27.770 --> 00:08:31.150
Unlike you, I don't have anything I want to do.

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:44.370
It's no use, I just can't get it!

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:53.590
I wonder if Mao-neechan will be back soon.

00:08:53.590 --> 00:08:54.760
I'm home!

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:58.760
You're sure late, where did you go?

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:01.520
Yeah, just around.

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:03.270
Could it have been a date?

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:06.020
Would you be jealous if it was?

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:07.940
Who would?

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:11.320
As the little brother, I'm just worried about my sister.

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:13.690
Well, thank you for the hard work.

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:16.660
Ah, Mao-neechan!

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:21.030
There's a math problem I don't understand.

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:22.370
Could you help me?

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:27.210
It's second year math, so it must be simple for you, right?

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:29.540
You also studied a lot during middle school.

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:34.380
Ah, no, that's a bit...

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:37.590
Just think of it as doing it for your cute little brother.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:39.600
Please.

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:44.560
Um, Kouichi, I'm not the same as I was during middle school.

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:49.560
Eh, you came to hate studying?!

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:51.690
Shh, your voice is too loud!

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:54.610
But, you were...

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:56.650
Certain Victory

00:09:55.530 --> 00:09:58.780
Well, people change after two years.

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:00.490
What happened?

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:05.660
You know that I took an entrance exam for Kitazuiryou High School, right?

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:09.420
Yeah, that super prestigious school.

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:11.380
I didn't hear the details though.

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:14.550
I <i>really </i>studied for it.

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:16.630
I even went as far as not sleeping!

00:10:18.470 --> 00:10:24.600
Yet, of all the days, I caught influenza on the day of the entrance test.

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:32.110
I had a temperature of 40°C, and my head was spinning.

00:10:32.110 --> 00:10:36.320
In the end, my answers were all off in the answer column.

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:47.000
Ever since then, I've never been motivated enough.

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:51.120
During class, I mostly sleep or read a book.

00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:54.000
I haven't studied for the upcoming test either.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:55.340
I have no confidence.

00:10:56.800 --> 00:11:00.930
And so, I don't think I can help you with math.

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:01.590
Sorry.

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:04.600
If it's about love, I'll help you anytime.

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:20.820
Mao-neechan did, huh?

00:11:21.570 --> 00:11:24.320
She was such a nerd during middle school though.

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:27.540
It seems like she seriously has no motivation at all.

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:30.500
It's already the third day of the test period.

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:32.250
All she does is play games.

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:34.630
Is she going to be okay?

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:35.170
Hey.

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:41.130
I'm sorry to interrupt your conversation, but could you help me with this?

00:11:41.590 --> 00:11:44.550
Ah, that's impossible, I'm an idiot.

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:45.890
You're asking the wrong person.

00:11:46.310 --> 00:11:47.390
Same on the left.

00:11:50.270 --> 00:11:51.100
I see.

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:54.270
What's wrong?

00:11:54.940 --> 00:11:58.320
I might have to stop playing soccer.

00:11:58.730 --> 00:12:00.570
W-What's wrong so suddenly?

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:02.740
That's not like you, Sakino-san.

00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:05.450
That's right, what happened that would make you stop-

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:06.580
The other day, the teacher told me...

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:09.910
If I fail even one test next time,

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:12.460
he'll suspend me indefinitely from club activities.

00:12:13.370 --> 00:12:14.040
Are you serious?!

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:17.540
I've been studying for the last three days without sleep,

00:12:18.130 --> 00:12:20.760
but nothing is going into my head because of the pressure.

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:24.510
We have to do something about that.

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:27.430
We wont be much help to you though.

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:29.350
Ah!

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:31.060
I just thought of a great idea!

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:34.520
Mao-neechan!

00:12:35.520 --> 00:12:35.980
Yo.

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:37.810
Oh, what's up?

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:41.820
Hey, are you free after class ends?

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:43.780
Yeah, I don't really have any plans.

00:12:44.320 --> 00:12:48.370
Um, I thought I'd consult you about some love problems.

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:52.000
Oh, so you finally felt like coming to me!

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:54.040
Ah, that's not it.

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:55.460
It's not me but Kazuki.

00:12:56.120 --> 00:12:57.750
He says he wants a consultation from you.

00:12:58.380 --> 00:12:59.130
Kazuki wants...

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:00.380
So who is it?

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:01.920
W-Who knows?

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:05.050
I guess you'll find out if you ask him after school in the library.

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:07.180
I got it, I'll be there for sure!

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:08.890
I'll see you later then.

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:26.110
Are you okay? Let me help.

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:28.780
Thank you.

00:13:31.990 --> 00:13:33.000
Was it heavy?

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:34.080
I'm fine.

00:13:38.540 --> 00:13:40.590
Are you free after school?

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:41.170
Eh?

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:43.460
Everyone is going to be studying.

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:45.800
It'll be more fun with more people.

00:13:47.550 --> 00:13:49.090
If I won't be in the way then...

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:52.350
N-No way, you won't be in the way!

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:54.310
Well...

00:13:55.350 --> 00:13:56.480
Then, with pleasure.

00:13:56.770 --> 00:13:57.520
All right.

00:13:59.190 --> 00:14:02.190
About what you were discussing, please let me accompany you.

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:14.040
You said this was about a love problem.

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:17.960
Forgive me, Mao-neechan.

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:19.920
I thought you wouldn't come if I didn't tell you that.

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:21.330
That's right.

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:24.340
If you're going to worry, it's better to worry with everyone.

00:14:24.670 --> 00:14:27.380
That might be true, but...

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:29.760
Please, Mizusawa-senpai!

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:31.390
I have no where else to go!

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:33.310
Please help me study!

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:34.640
Asuka-chan...

00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:36.430
I don't want to stop playing soccer!

00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:40.150
If I'm okay with you then...

00:14:40.150 --> 00:14:42.310
I'm not sure if I'll be of any help though.

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:45.150
Here's the question:

00:14:45.480 --> 00:14:49.400
Who brought forth the idea that DNA is structured as a double-helix?

00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:52.200
Here! It was Watson and Crick!

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:55.200
You're a genius Juliet-chan!

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:58.080
I'll give you a kiss as a prize.

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:02.920
For this sentence, you start using an "S".

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:04.960
I see!

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:07.210
What's the mark for this question?

00:15:07.210 --> 00:15:10.880
Ah, for that, ask someone who understands, besides me.

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:12.510
Does that mean you don't get it?

00:15:12.510 --> 00:15:13.350
Well, yeah.

00:15:14.010 --> 00:15:18.520
Amazing, I couldn't do this problem the other day!

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:20.850
Your teaching method is really good.

00:15:21.350 --> 00:15:24.480
No, it's because you did your best, Asuka-chan.

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:27.780
Also, when I see you trying your best,

00:15:27.780 --> 00:15:29.280
I get motivated.

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:31.320
Senpai...

00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:35.780
All right, next is history, let's do our best!

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:40.750
That's my worst subject.

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:43.250
It goes in one ear and right out the other.

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:46.130
You can't even remember the approximate year?

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:49.090
Yes, I forget the time period itself.

00:15:49.590 --> 00:15:52.840
Things other than dates are even worse.

00:15:53.180 --> 00:15:54.260
I see.

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:56.350
That's a problem.

00:15:57.260 --> 00:15:57.930
Um...

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:01.810
How about associating it with something you like?

00:16:02.270 --> 00:16:03.350
Something we like?

00:16:03.770 --> 00:16:04.310
Yes.

00:16:04.860 --> 00:16:07.770
For Sakino-san, she would remember things by associating them to soccer.

00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:12.070
I remember things in history by associating them with books.

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:13.530
How?

00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:15.320
For example,

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:27.170
Hamlet

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:19.790
Hamlet was written in the 1600's, and that's when the battle of Sekigahara occurred.

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:27.170
Battle of Sekigahara

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:23.750
In 1885, the first prime minister of the cabinet was elected,

00:16:21.870 --> 00:16:27.170
The First Prime Minister of the Cabinet

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:26.330
and this is the same publication date as Nietzsche's book.

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:27.170
Nietzsche

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:28.920
It's a bit roundabout though.

00:16:29.210 --> 00:16:30.550
I see.

00:16:30.550 --> 00:16:32.260
That's kind of interesting.

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:35.680
So basically, I just have to associate everything to soccer, right?

00:16:36.180 --> 00:16:37.760
All right, I'm going to try it out!

00:16:39.930 --> 00:16:42.520
Let's make a good country! World cup!

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:42.520
Looks like it's coming along well.

00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:43.270
Yeah.

00:16:56.360 --> 00:16:57.200
Futami-san!

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:02.870
She was in the nurse's office.

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:08.040
If you'd like, how about studying together?

00:17:08.540 --> 00:17:09.380
Me?

00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:10.550
U-Um...

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:12.880
You're smart,

00:17:13.420 --> 00:17:16.380
so maybe you could help us study.

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:19.850
You can't accept that you can't do it?

00:17:25.560 --> 00:17:26.810
Hold on!

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:29.190
What's with that attitude?

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:36.150
Not everyone is as smart as you.

00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:52.800
Sorry, sorry, the mood just went kind of sour.

00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:54.010
Let's keep going.

00:17:56.470 --> 00:17:59.180
Kouichi, that girl was Futami-san, right?

00:17:59.590 --> 00:18:00.680
Is she smart?

00:18:00.680 --> 00:18:01.850
What are you saying?

00:18:01.850 --> 00:18:03.600
She's a genius with an IQ of 190.

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:05.180
Eh, I see.

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:07.810
Did I say something bad?

00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:13.360
Futami-san!

00:18:16.030 --> 00:18:16.530
I'm sorry.

00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:17.650
About what?

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:18.700
Eh?

00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:31.080
Well then, I'm taking the train.

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:35.300
Kouichi, don't become a wolf when seeing her off.

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:36.300
Who would?!

00:18:37.050 --> 00:18:38.090
Let's go, Hoshino-san.

00:18:38.550 --> 00:18:39.340
O-Okay.

00:18:40.050 --> 00:18:40.760
Later.

00:18:43.850 --> 00:18:45.850
Be careful, Yuumi-chan!

00:18:49.810 --> 00:18:51.230
They're in their springtime of youth.

00:18:51.690 --> 00:18:53.230
Love-love!

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:56.110
Let's go then!

00:18:59.990 --> 00:19:03.530
Mizusawa-senpai sure is a wonderful person, huh?

00:19:03.530 --> 00:19:04.580
Mao-neechan?

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:05.580
Yeah.

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:10.500
Because, even though she said she doesn't like studying,

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:12.580
she helped Sakino-san study.

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:15.880
She's always been smart.

00:19:16.840 --> 00:19:19.380
You're childhood friends, right?

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:22.680
Kazuki and I used to play with her in the past.

00:19:23.300 --> 00:19:26.970
She moved to France two years ago and I hadn't seen her since,

00:19:26.970 --> 00:19:29.060
but now she's freeloading at my house.

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:35.520
Well, she kind of feels like an older sister to Kazuki and me, I guess.

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:37.030
I see.

00:19:37.780 --> 00:19:42.110
You and Mizusawa-senpai get along very well, so I thought...

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:43.990
Eh, that's not it!

00:19:43.990 --> 00:19:45.990
That's definitely not true!

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:46.490
Really.

00:19:48.910 --> 00:19:51.920
That's surprising, I didn't think we were looked at that way.

00:19:58.880 --> 00:19:59.630
Yahoo!

00:20:04.430 --> 00:20:09.020
And so, for Asuka-chan and my sake, everyone held a study group.

00:20:09.020 --> 00:20:11.480
Thanks to them, I feel kind of motivated now.

00:20:13.690 --> 00:20:16.110
Huh, is this boring?

00:20:16.110 --> 00:20:16.690
Not really.

00:20:17.230 --> 00:20:17.940
Really?

00:20:20.740 --> 00:20:21.320
The consultation.

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:24.950
You could've consulted with me,

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:26.570
about studying for the test.

00:20:29.240 --> 00:20:33.670
Sorry, but I thought you didn't like talking about studying.

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:48.810
Amazing, you're in the top ten, Mao-neechan!

00:20:49.310 --> 00:20:52.230
I felt kind of motivated thanks to everyone.

00:20:52.230 --> 00:20:53.560
I'm still in rehab though.

00:20:54.060 --> 00:20:54.850
Thanks.

00:20:56.060 --> 00:20:57.770
You're in rehab and you got this?

00:20:57.770 --> 00:20:59.570
Mizusawa-senpai!

00:21:01.940 --> 00:21:03.450
Thank you!

00:21:03.450 --> 00:21:06.070
Thanks to you, I didn't fail any tests!

00:21:06.490 --> 00:21:09.080
I see, I'm glad, congratulations!

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:11.240
You'll be able to play soccer again now.

00:21:11.240 --> 00:21:11.700
Yes!

00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:15.040
This is my first failed test...

00:21:15.040 --> 00:21:17.830
I guess this is what you call a high school ordeal.

00:21:18.710 --> 00:21:20.500
I wonder how Futami-san did?

00:21:21.170 --> 00:21:23.170
Futami Eriko

00:21:21.170 --> 00:21:23.170
Yamaguchi Tarou

00:21:21.170 --> 00:21:23.170
Saitou Mitsuki

00:21:21.170 --> 00:21:23.170
Tanaka Kazuo

00:21:21.170 --> 00:21:23.170
Class

00:21:26.130 --> 00:21:28.930
You can aim for the top next time, Mao-neechan.

00:21:30.220 --> 00:21:31.810
That's impossible.

00:21:32.640 --> 00:21:34.890
kowaresou de

00:21:32.640 --> 00:21:34.890
It looks like it’s about to fall apart.

00:21:34.480 --> 00:21:35.640
Sorry, Mao-neechan.

00:21:35.230 --> 00:21:38.860
taisetsu sugite sawarenakatta

00:21:35.230 --> 00:21:38.860
So precious that I couldn’t touch it.

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:37.810
Hoshino-san!

00:21:38.480 --> 00:21:39.150
How was it?

00:21:39.190 --> 00:21:41.570
wasarenai yo

00:21:39.190 --> 00:21:41.570
I won’t forget

00:21:42.610 --> 00:21:47.320
hoshi ni negai o

00:21:42.610 --> 00:21:47.320
that wish upon a star.

00:21:55.540 --> 00:22:00.040
kyou shitsu no sumi ni wa itsumo fushigi bako

00:21:55.540 --> 00:22:00.040
The strange box lying in the corner of the classroom;

00:22:00.080 --> 00:22:02.420
dare ni mo misenai shi

00:22:00.080 --> 00:22:02.420
I won’t show it to anyone.

00:22:02.800 --> 00:22:05.220
itsumo minai furi

00:22:02.800 --> 00:22:05.220
I always pretend not to see it.

00:22:06.550 --> 00:22:11.140
hajimete okutte moratta hoshi no yoru

00:22:06.550 --> 00:22:11.140
The first time you walked me home during that starry night.

00:22:11.140 --> 00:22:13.520
ano kajitsu mo

00:22:11.140 --> 00:22:13.520
The fruit

00:22:13.930 --> 00:22:16.100
mada tabetenai kedo

00:22:13.930 --> 00:22:16.100
I have not eaten.

00:22:16.640 --> 00:22:18.940
honki de butsukatta

00:22:16.640 --> 00:22:18.940
I struck it with all my might.

00:22:19.520 --> 00:22:21.730
naite sawaida

00:22:19.520 --> 00:22:21.730
I cried and I screamed.

00:22:21.940 --> 00:22:30.240
shinkei wa kitto kinui totokoutetsu de dekiteta

00:22:21.940 --> 00:22:30.240
I’m certain nerves are made from silk and steel.

00:22:30.570 --> 00:22:32.870
osaekirenai

00:22:30.570 --> 00:22:32.870
My insuppressible feelings

00:22:33.160 --> 00:22:36.870
omoi o nagete negai boshi ni

00:22:33.160 --> 00:22:36.870
are cast on a wishing star.

00:22:37.120 --> 00:22:38.500
ima kakeru yo

00:22:37.120 --> 00:22:38.500
It’s now time to run.

00:22:38.670 --> 00:22:41.920
tobira no soto wa DAIAMONDO

00:22:38.670 --> 00:22:41.920
Beyond the door are diamonds.

00:22:41.960 --> 00:22:47.880
ikusen no yume kaki utsushita NOOTO ni

00:22:41.960 --> 00:22:47.880
Thousands of dreams transcribed onto a notebook.

00:22:48.130 --> 00:22:52.970
tojikometara ai ni yuku yo

00:22:48.130 --> 00:22:52.970
Whenever I’m trapped I’m go see you.

00:22:52.970 --> 00:22:58.940
kirakira toeien o kiritotta mamade

00:22:52.970 --> 00:22:58.940
The sparkle and eternity are cut short.

00:22:59.190 --> 00:23:03.900
yakusoku shita kimi to nara ano hi no KISU o

00:22:59.190 --> 00:23:03.900
We made a promise with a kiss on that day.

00:23:04.020 --> 00:23:05.940
kowaresou de

00:23:04.020 --> 00:23:05.940
It looks like it’s about to fall apart.

00:23:06.230 --> 00:23:09.900
taisetsu sugite sawarenakatta

00:23:06.230 --> 00:23:09.900
So precious that I couldn’t touch it.

00:23:10.200 --> 00:23:12.990
wasurenai yo

00:23:10.200 --> 00:23:12.990
I won’t forget

00:23:13.660 --> 00:23:18.960
hoshi ni negai o

00:23:13.660 --> 00:23:18.960
that wish upon a star.

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:39.980
Next Episode

00:23:25.460 --> 00:23:27.420
Ah, Greetings. This is Hiiragi Akira.

00:23:27.420 --> 00:23:32.000
With midterms over, our Movie Research Club is finally becoming serious in creating a movie.

00:23:32.090 --> 00:23:33.590
The problem is, who will play as the heroine?

00:23:33.890 --> 00:23:38.530
This is where I can show my skills as the leader.
